The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the changes made to src/commands_web.rs:

1. **Added `ddg_search(query, max_results)` function** — Performs a DuckDuckGo search by URL-encoding the query, fetching from https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/?q=..., and parsing results with the existing parse_ddg_results function.

2. Modified `web_search(query, max_results)` — Now checks if EXA_API_KEY is set and non-empty. If yes, calls exa_search(). If not, falls back to ddg_search().

3. Modified `web_search_and_read(query, max_results)` — When Exa key is present, tries Exa first. If Exa fails for any reason (network error, rate limit, etc.), falls back to DuckDuckGo as a second attempt. When no Exa key is set, uses DDG directly.

4. Removed `#[allow(dead_code)]` from parse_ddg_results since it's now actively used by ddg_search.

5. **Added 4 tests:**
   • test_web_search_uses_ddg_when_exa_key_unset — Verifies no EXA_API_KEY error when key is unset
   • `test_web_search_fallback_path_selection` — Verifies DDG path is selected when Exa key missing
   • test_ddg_search_returns_results_from_html — Unit test for DDG parsing via the search function
   • test_web_search_and_read_no_exa_key_no_panic — Verifies `web_search_and_read` doesn't panic or require EXA key
